---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"

const html =
  '<p>Koakademy provides a grading and academic performance engine that balances flexibility for faculty with strict audit compliance and institutional verification.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Supported Grading Systems</h2>\n<p>Koakademy supports multiple concurrent grading standards configured per program, school, or department (<code>GradingPolicy</code> and <code>GradingPolicyVersion</code>):</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Grading Scale</th>\n<th>Format / Range</th>\n<th>Typical Institutional Usage</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Philippine Collegiate Standard</strong></td>\n<td><code>1.00</code> (Highest / Excellent) to <code>3.00</code> (Passing), <code>5.00</code> (Failed)</td>\n<td>State universities, private colleges, CHED degree programs.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Percentage Scale</strong></td>\n<td><code>0%</code> to <code>100%</code>, with passing thresholds at <code>75%</code> or <code>60%</code></td>\n<td>Junior &amp; Senior High Schools (DepEd K-12), preparatory institutions.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>US / International Letter Scale</strong></td>\n<td><code>A+</code>, <code>A</code>, <code>A-</code>, <code>B+</code>, <code>B</code>, <code>B-</code>, <code>C</code>, <code>D</code>, <code>F</code></td>\n<td>International programs, graduate business schools.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Competency / Rubric Standard</strong></td>\n<td><code>Competent</code> (C), <code>Not Yet Competent</code> (NYC)</td>\n<td>TESDA technical-vocational qualifications.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Qualitative / Pass-Fail</strong></td>\n<td><code>P</code> (Passed), <code>F</code> (Failed), <code>INC</code> (Incomplete), <code>DRP</code> (Dropped)</td>\n<td>Thesis defense, physical education, internships, residency.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>Faculty Grade Encoding &amp; Verification Workflow</h2>\n<pre><code>┌─────────────────────┐\n│ 1. Submission Window│\n│    Opens (Schedule) │\n└──────────┬──────────┘\n           │\n           ▼\n┌─────────────────────┐       [Autosaved Draft]       ┌─────────────────────┐\n│ 2. Faculty Portal   │ ────────────────────────────▶ │ Working Draft Sheet │\n│    Grade Input      │                               │ (Not Yet Final)     │\n└──────────┬──────────┘                               └─────────────────────┘\n           │\n           ▼\n┌─────────────────────┐\n│ 3. Submit &amp; Sign-off│\n│    (Review Summary) │\n└──────────┬──────────┘\n           │\n           ▼\n┌─────────────────────┐\n│ 4. Dean / Registrar │\n│    Verification     │\n└──────────┬──────────┘\n           │\n           ▼\n┌─────────────────────┐\n│ 5. Locked &amp; Visible │\n│    in Student Portal│\n└─────────────────────┘\n</code></pre>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Submission Window Control:</strong> Registrars define opening and closing deadlines for Midterm and Final grade encoding with automatic countdown alerts for faculty.</li>\n<li><strong>Draft Autosave:</strong> Faculty can enter grades incrementally. Grades remain in draft status, invisible to students, until formal submission.</li>\n<li><strong>Formal Verification:</strong> Once submitted, grades require electronic verification from the Department Chair or College Dean.</li>\n<li><strong>Immutable Locking:</strong> Verified grades are locked against tampering. Any subsequent modification requires an authorized, audited <strong>Change of Grade Request</strong> with documented justifications.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2>General Weighted Average (GWA) Engine</h2>\n<p>Koakademy computes students&#39; cumulative and term General Weighted Average in real time:</p>\n<pre><code class="language-txt">GWA = Sum(Final Grade × Credit Units) / Sum(Credit Units)\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Configurable Subject Exclusions</h3>\n<p>Certain curricular subjects should not impact academic honors or cumulative academic standing:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>National Service Training Program (NSTP / CWTS / ROTC):</strong> Fully recorded for graduation requirements but excluded from collegiate GPA/GWA calculations per CHED regulations.</li>\n<li><strong>Physical Education (PE):</strong> Optionally excluded or included based on institutional policy.</li>\n<li><strong>Remedial / Bridging Courses:</strong> Non-credit foundation courses tracked separately from graduation credit totals.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Academic Honors &amp; Deans List</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Automated Deans List:</strong> Automatically identifies eligible students per semester who satisfy minimum load requirements (e.g. at least 15 academic units), achieve a minimum GWA (e.g. 1.75 or higher), and have no grade below 2.50 or any Incomplete marks.</li>\n<li><strong>Latin Honors Calculation:</strong> Evaluates graduating seniors against institutional Latin Honors criteria:<ul>\n<li><em>Summa Cum Laude:</em> GWA 1.00 – 1.20 (no grade below 2.00)</li>\n<li><em>Magna Cum Laude:</em> GWA 1.21 – 1.45 (no grade below 2.25)</li>\n<li><em>Cum Laude:</em> GWA 1.46 – 1.75 (no grade below 2.50)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>Official Transcript of Records (TOR) Generation</h2>\n<p>Koakademy renders official Transcripts of Records directly as high-resolution PDF documents via the Gotenberg engine:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Security Watermarking:</strong> Anti-fraud background patterns and institutional seals.</li>\n<li><strong>Accredited Layout:</strong> Multi-page tabular layout displaying course codes, descriptive titles, final grades, completion terms, and credit units earned.</li>\n<li><strong>Signatory Blocks:</strong> Automated positioning of Registrar, College Dean, and University President signature blocks.</li>\n<li><strong>Cryptographic Verification Hash:</strong> A SHA-256 integrity hash is embedded in the document header and rendered as a QR code, allowing third-party employers and foreign universities to verify document authenticity online.</li>\n</ul>\n'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Grading Workflows, Policies & Transcripts"
  path="/docs/features/grading-transcripts"
  description="In-depth documentation of grade encoding, multi-system grading scales, automated GWA calculation, and verifiable Transcript of Records."
>
  <Fragment set:html={html} />
</DocsLayout>
